11 0 obj
<< /Length 2789 >>
stream
BT
/F1 9 Tf 50 780 Td (PMFBY Operational Guidelines \(2023\) ? Section VIII: Premium Rates and Subsidy) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 758 Tm /F2 12 Tf ([SECTION: Section VIII \(Clause 13.1\)] Maximum Insurance Charges \(Premium\) Payable by Farmer) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 740 Tm /F1 10 Tf ([PARA | SEC=Section VIII \(Clause 13.1\)] The Actuarial Premium Rate \(APR\) is charged by the implementing insurance company as determined by competitive bidding. However, the maximum insurance charges \(premium\) payable by the farmer under PMFBY \(2023 Operational Guidelines\) are strictly capped according to season and crop category as specified in Table 1 below:) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 724 Tm /F2 10 Tf ([TABLE_START | ID=TBL_OG2023_PREMIUM_RATES | SEC=Section VIII \(Clause 13.1, Table 1\) | CAPTION=Table 1: Season-wise Maximum Insurance Charges \(Premium\) Payable by Farmer under PMFBY \(2023 Guidelines\)]) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 710 Tm /F2 10 Tf ([TABLE_HEADERS | ID=TBL_OG2023_PREMIUM_RATES] S.No. | Season | Crop Category / Crops Covered | Maximum Insurance Charges Payable by Farmer \(% of Sum Insured\) | Mandatory Qualification / Condition) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 696 Tm /F1 9 Tf ([TABLE_ROW | ID=TBL_OG2023_PREMIUM_RATES | ROW=TBL_OG2023_PREMIUM_RATES_R1] 1 | Kharif | All food grain and oilseed crops \(all cereals, millets, pulses, and oilseeds\) | 2.0% of Sum Insured | 2.0% of Sum Insured or Actuarial rate, whichever is less) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 683 Tm /F1 9 Tf ([TABLE_ROW | ID=TBL_OG2023_PREMIUM_RATES | ROW=TBL_OG2023_PREMIUM_RATES_R2] 2 | Rabi | All food grain and oilseed crops \(all cereals, millets, pulses, and oilseeds\) | 1.5% of Sum Insured | 1.5% of Sum Insured or Actuarial rate, whichever is less) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 670 Tm /F1 9 Tf ([TABLE_ROW | ID=TBL_OG2023_PREMIUM_RATES | ROW=TBL_OG2023_PREMIUM_RATES_R3] 3 | Kharif and Rabi \(Annual\) | Annual commercial and annual horticultural crops \(and perennial horticultural crops on pilot basis\) | 5.0% of Sum Insured | 5.0% of Sum Insured or Actuarial rate, whichever is less) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 657 Tm /F2 10 Tf ([TABLE_END | ID=TBL_OG2023_PREMIUM_RATES]) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 641 Tm /F1 10 Tf ([PARA | SEC=Section VIII \(Clause 13.2\)] Important Rule on Qualification and Basis: In all three categories of Table 1, the stated percentage \(2.0% for Kharif food grain and oilseed crops, 1.5% for Rabi food grain and oilseed crops, and 5.0% for annual commercial and annual horticultural crops\) is a maximum ceiling expressed as a percentage of Sum Insured \(SI\), subject to the mandatory qualification 'or Actuarial rate, whichever is less'. If the bidding actuarial rate for a crop is lower than the prescribed ceiling \(for example, 1.2% for a Kharif food grain\), the farmer pays the lower actuarial rate \(1.2%\), not 2.0%.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 40 Tm /F1 9 Tf ([PRINTED_PAGE: 2]) Tj
ET
endstream
