/F1 9 Tf 50 780 Td (PMFBY Operational Guidelines \(2023\) ? Section VIII: Premium Subsidy Sharing & Ceilings) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 758 Tm /F2 12 Tf ([SECTION: Section VIII \(Clause 13.3\)] Central and State Government Premium Subsidy Sharing and Actuarial Rate Ceilings) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 740 Tm /F1 10 Tf ([PARA | SEC=Section VIII \(Clause 13.3\)] The difference between the Actuarial Premium Rate \(APR\) and the maximum insurance charges payable by farmers is treated as the Normal Premium Subsidy. Under the 2023 Revamped Operational Guidelines, Central Government premium subsidy is subject to explicit actuarial premium rate ceilings and regional sharing ratios detailed in Table 2:) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 724 Tm /F2 10 Tf ([TABLE_START | ID=TBL_OG2023_SUBSIDY_CAPS | SEC=Section VIII \(Clause 13.3, Table 2\) | CAPTION=Table 2: Premium Subsidy Sharing Pattern and Central Subsidy Actuarial Ceilings \(2023 Guidelines\)]) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 710 Tm /F2 10 Tf ([TABLE_HEADERS | ID=TBL_OG2023_SUBSIDY_CAPS] Rule Parameter | Applicable Category / Geography | Prescribed Numerical Value / Ratio | Basis / Denominator | Qualification and Operational Condition) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 696 Tm /F1 9 Tf ([TABLE_ROW | ID=TBL_OG2023_SUBSIDY_CAPS | ROW=TBL_OG2023_SUBSIDY_CAPS_R1] Central Subsidy Actuarial Ceiling \(Unirrigated\) | Unirrigated \(Rainfed\) areas/crops \(districts with less than 50% irrigated area\) | 30.0% | Actuarial Premium Rate \(% of Sum Insured\) | Central Government subsidy is capped for actuarial premium rates up to 30.0%; subsidy above 30.0% is borne by the State/UT) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 683 Tm /F1 9 Tf ([TABLE_ROW | ID=TBL_OG2023_SUBSIDY_CAPS | ROW=TBL_OG2023_SUBSIDY_CAPS_R2] Central Subsidy Actuarial Ceiling \(Irrigated\) | Irrigated areas/crops \(districts with 50.0% or more irrigated area\) | 25.0% | Actuarial Premium Rate \(% of Sum Insured\) | Central Government subsidy is capped for actuarial premium rates up to 25.0%; subsidy above 25.0% is borne by the State/UT) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 670 Tm /F1 9 Tf ([TABLE_ROW | ID=TBL_OG2023_SUBSIDY_CAPS | ROW=TBL_OG2023_SUBSIDY_CAPS_R3] Normal Premium Subsidy Sharing \(General States\) | All General States and Union Territories \(excluding North Eastern Region\) | 50:50 \(50.0% Central share, 50.0% State share\) | Balance Normal Premium Subsidy | Shared equally \(50.0% Central Government and 50.0% State Government\) up to the 25%/30% actuarial ceiling) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 657 Tm /F1 9 Tf ([TABLE_ROW | ID=TBL_OG2023_SUBSIDY_CAPS | ROW=TBL_OG2023_SUBSIDY_CAPS_R4] Normal Premium Subsidy Sharing \(North Eastern States\) | North Eastern Region \(NER\) States and Himalayan States as notified | 90:10 \(90.0% Central share, 10.0% State share\) | Balance Normal Premium Subsidy | 90.0% paid by Central Government and 10.0% paid by North Eastern State Government up to the actuarial ceiling) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 644 Tm /F2 10 Tf ([TABLE_END | ID=TBL_OG2023_SUBSIDY_CAPS]) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 40 Tm /F1 9 Tf ([PRINTED_PAGE: 3]) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
