/F1 9 Tf 50 780 Td (PMFBY Operational Guidelines \(2023\) ? Section XVI: Seasonality Discipline & Penalties) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 758 Tm /F2 12 Tf ([SECTION: Section XVI \(Clause 16\)] Seasonality Discipline, Cut-Off Dates, Administrative Expenses, and Penal Interest) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 740 Tm /F2 10 Tf ([TABLE_START | ID=TBL_OG2023_TIMELINES_PENALTIES | SEC=Section XVI \(Clause 16.1-17.4, Table 4\) | CAPTION=Table 4: Operational Cut-Off Dates, Penal Interest, and Administrative Expense Ceilings \(2023 Guidelines\)]) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 726 Tm /F2 10 Tf ([TABLE_HEADERS | ID=TBL_OG2023_TIMELINES_PENALTIES] Operational Rule | Season / Stakeholder | Numerical Value | Unit / Basis | Qualification / Condition) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 712 Tm /F1 9 Tf ([TABLE_ROW | ID=TBL_OG2023_TIMELINES_PENALTIES | ROW=TBL_OG2023_TIMELINES_PENALTIES_R1] Delayed Claim Settlement / Delayed Subsidy Penal Interest | Insurance Companies and State Governments | 12.0% | % per annum \(simple interest on delayed claim/subsidy amount\) | Insurance companies must pay 12.0% per annum interest to farmers for claim delays beyond prescribed cut-off \(21 days after receipt of yield data/subsidy\); States pay 12.0% interest for subsidy delays) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 699 Tm /F1 9 Tf ([TABLE_ROW | ID=TBL_OG2023_TIMELINES_PENALTIES | ROW=TBL_OG2023_TIMELINES_PENALTIES_R2] Claim Settlement Timeline after Yield Data & Subsidy Receipt | Implementing Insurance Companies | 21 days | Days from receipt of yield data and premium subsidy | Claims must be settled within 21 days \(3 weeks\) after receipt of both final yield data and Central/State subsidy share) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 686 Tm /F1 9 Tf ([TABLE_ROW | ID=TBL_OG2023_TIMELINES_PENALTIES | ROW=TBL_OG2023_TIMELINES_PENALTIES_R3] Bank / Channel Partner Portal Data Upload Window | Commercial Banks, RRBs, Cooperative Banks, CSCs | 15 days | Days after enrolment cut-off date | Banks must upload individual farmer proposal details on National Crop Insurance Portal \(NCIP\) within 15 days of cut-off date for Kharif/Rabi) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 673 Tm /F1 9 Tf ([TABLE_ROW | ID=TBL_OG2023_TIMELINES_PENALTIES | ROW=TBL_OG2023_TIMELINES_PENALTIES_R4] IEC and Administrative Expense Allocation | Implementing Agencies and States | 0.5% | % of Gross Premium | 0.5% of gross premium collected is earmarked exclusively for Information, Education and Communication \(IEC\) and capacity-building activities) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 660 Tm /F2 10 Tf ([TABLE_END | ID=TBL_OG2023_TIMELINES_PENALTIES]) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 644 Tm /F1 10 Tf ([PARA | SEC=Section XVI \(Clause 16.2\)] Standard Enrolment Cut-Off Dates: Unless specifically varied by State notification within the permissible window, the standard final cut-off date for farmer enrolment and premium debit is 31st July for the Kharif season and 31st December for the Rabi season.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 628 Tm /F1 10 Tf ([PARA | SEC=Section XIX \(Clause 19.3 - CCE & Outreach Distractor Paragraph\)] Operational Sampling and Outreach Benchmarks: For estimation of crop yield at the Gram Panchayat \(Insurance Unit\) level, a minimum of 4 Crop Cutting Experiments \(CCEs\) are mandatory for major crops, and 8 CCEs are required at the Mandal/Taluka level. Under the National Crop Insurance Portal outreach drive \(Krishi Rakshak Helpline 14447\), field agencies target at least 30% participation from women cultivators and small/marginal farmers holding less than 2.0 hectares of operational land, with digital village camps covering 5% of high-priority blocks each week. \(Note: The 30% women outreach target, 2.0 hectares small-farmer landholding threshold, and 5% weekly block camp coverage are administrative outreach targets, NOT farmer insurance premium rates.\)) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 40 Tm /F1 9 Tf ([PRINTED_PAGE: 5]) Tj
